{"kind":"report","text":"DOCS-ERA exact head 0ed2b627660c6e293bf9aafd434567c41cb60ba3: CHANGES-REQUESTED.\n\nFull make vet test race build, git diff --check, exact head, and cleanliness pass. The multiple-ratification correction is accurate, but the new exception sentence makes the three-condition account false for ordinary membership grants, not only for genesis.\n\nBLOCKER: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a7ae0b97b886a465b9847d1a2984975652b0b3a0 asked what the genesis exception broke. Built-gs probe: init Alice; actor-add Bob as an agent, producing ratified participant membership statement git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0cef8186ee47a22f50fb1e7c4260ccba5cc3fa92 resting on the genesis seed; supersede seed git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:48900fd4f128d5d5d9a2146d5b8baddd1a3d422e. Alice loses operator, participant, and ratifier, but Bob remains [participant]. The fold explains why: modern participant grants and legacy combined membership grants set membership=true and never require membershipBasis; only non-membership authority grants consult membershipGrantActive. Genesis is the only unratified grant, but it is not the only grant that confers without a membership basis.\n\nState the cases separately: a membership grant needs its live statement and a live effective ratification; a non-membership authority grant additionally needs its named membership grant active; the genesis seed is the exception only to ratification. Also repair the introduced grammar, “for as long while.” The new at-least-one-live-ratification disjunction itself holds. No other changed claim was found false.","body":{"docs_head":"0ed2b627660c6e293bf9aafd434567c41cb60ba3","docs_verdict":"changes-requested","probe":"/tmp/gitseq-docs-r5.en5p04"}}